## 2. Missing International Blocks — Priority Additions

### 2.1 Historical Blocs (Critical Gap)

Only **one** block carries `status: historical` (GATT) — a severe underrepresentation. The Cold War era produced multiple major alliances that shaped the modern world and belong in any complete geopolitical reference database.

| Suggested ID | Name | Type | Period | Members |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `WARSAWPACT` | Warsaw Pact / Warsaw Treaty Organization | military, political | 1955–1991 | 8 (Soviet-led Eastern Bloc) |
| `SEATO` | Southeast Asia Treaty Organization | military | 1954–1977 | 8 (US, UK, France, Australia, NZ, Pakistan, Philippines, Thailand) |
| `CENTO` | Central Treaty Organization (Baghdad Pact) | military | 1955–1979 | 5 (UK, Turkey, Iraq, Iran, Pakistan) |

Additionally, **NAFTA** (`status: formal`) and **TPP** exist in the database but should carry `status: historical` since both have been superseded (by USMCA and CPTPP respectively).

### 2.2 Recent Geopolitical Formations (2020–2025)

These are active, significant groupings formed in the last five years that are entirely absent:

| Suggested ID | Name | Blocktype(s) | Founded | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `IPEF` | Indo-Pacific Economic Framework | economic, trade | 2022 | US-led, 14 members covering 40% of global GDP |
| `EPC2022` | European Political Community (2022 revival) | political, forum | 2022 | Macron-initiated; 47 European states including non-EU members |
| `MSP` | Minerals Security Partnership | economic | 2022 | 14 countries + EU; critical minerals supply chain |
| `GLOBALGATEWAY` | Global Gateway | economic, project | 2021 | EU's €300B global infrastructure investment initiative |
| `PGII` | Partnership for Global Infrastructure and Investment | economic, project | 2022 | G7 infrastructure initiative, formerly Build Back Better World (B3W) |
